WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.107
The broadest split is categorical versus numeric.

00:00:03.107 --> 00:00:07.187
Categorical variables represent labels or ordered levels.

00:00:07.187 --> 00:00:09.662
Nominal and ordinal belong here.

00:00:09.662 --> 00:00:15.352
Numeric variables represent quantities. Interval and ratio belong here.

00:00:15.352 --> 00:00:19.392
Do not decide by looking only at the characters in the column.

00:00:19.392 --> 00:00:23.202
A ZIP code contains digits but is categorical.

00:00:23.202 --> 00:00:28.957
A satisfaction score uses numbers but usually represents ordered categories.

00:00:28.957 --> 00:00:36.377
Connect this idea to a university analyzing student records, surveys, and learning-platform activity.

00:00:36.377 --> 00:00:42.262
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:42.262 --> 00:00:49.827
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:49.827 --> 00:00:55.657
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:55.657 --> 00:01:01.609
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
